크라머<rsq/>s 규칙에 의해 <m>x_j</m>의 <m>i</m>번째 성분은 <m>\det(A_i)/\det(A)</m>이며, 여기서 <m>A_i</m>는 <m>A</m>의 <m>i</m>번째 열을 <m>e_j</m>로 바꾸어 <m>A</m>로부터 얻은 행렬입니다: <me>
          A_i = \mat{
            a_{11} a_{12} 0 a_{14};
            a_{21} a_{22} 1 a_{24};
            a_{31} a_{32} 0 a_{34};
            a_{41} a_{42} 0 a_{44}}
          \qquad(i = 3,\, j = 2).
        </me>

segments.source:
Therefore, the <m>j</m>th column of <m>A\inv</m> is
        <me>
          x_j = \frac 1{\det(A)}\vec{C_{j1} C_{j2} \vdots, C_{jn}},
        </me>
        and thus
        <me>
          A\inv = \mat{| | ,, |; x_1 x_2 \cdots, x_n; | | ,, |}
          = \frac 1{\det(A)}\mat{C_{11} C_{21} \cdots, C_{n-1,1} C_{n1};
                 C_{12} C_{22} \cdots, C_{n-1,2} C_{n2};
                 \vdots, \vdots, \ddots, \vdots, \vdots;
                 C_{1,n-1} C_{2,n-1} \cdots, C_{n-1,n-1} C_{n,n-1};
                 C_{1n} C_{2n} \cdots, C_{n-1,n} C_{nn}}.
        </me>

